# Copy this file to backend/.env and fill in the values:
#
#   Copy-Item .env.example .env     (Windows PowerShell)
#   cp .env.example .env            (macOS / Linux)
#
# .env is git-ignored; this example is committed as documentation of the keys.
# The backend reads it automatically at startup, so every terminal you launch
# the server from picks these up — there is no need to export them by hand.
#
# A real environment variable always overrides this file. That is how
# deployment stays correct: Render sets these in the process environment and no
# .env file exists there, so this can never shadow production configuration.

# PostgreSQL connection string.
#
# Leave it UNSET and the application still runs — search, docking, the 3D
# viewer and the PDF export all work, you simply cannot log in or store
# history. That is deliberate, so nobody is blocked waiting for credentials.
#
# Local development, using docker-compose.yml at the repository root:
#   DATABASE_URL=postgresql://postgres:postgres@localhost:5433/drugrepurposing
#
# Production (Neon): use the POOLED connection string, the one with "-pooler"
# in the hostname. Pooling matters because the backend can restart or run more
# than one instance, and each would otherwise open its own connections.
DATABASE_URL=

# Signing key for access tokens. Anyone holding it can forge a token for any
# account, so treat it exactly like the database password: it belongs here or
# in the hosting provider's secret settings, never in committed code.
#
# Generate one with:
#   python -c "import secrets; print(secrets.token_urlsafe(48))"
#
# If unset, a random key is generated at startup and every restart signs
# everyone out. Acceptable locally; not acceptable in deployment.
JWT_SECRET=

# How long a session lasts before the user must sign in again.
# Defaults to 10080 minutes (7 days).
# JWT_EXPIRE_MINUTES=10080

# Comma-separated list of frontend origins allowed to call this API.
# Left commented out it means "*", which is fine locally and wrong in
# production. Uncomment and set it to your deployed frontend URL there.
# ALLOWED_ORIGINS=https://your-app.vercel.app

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# LIVE BIOMEDICAL LOOKUPS
#
# The pipeline enriches results from Europe PMC while the user waits. Those
# calls are optional - screening, ranking, docking, history and similarity all
# work without them - and every one is bounded by a wall-clock budget, so a
# slow or unreachable API degrades the result rather than hanging the request.
#
# Set DISABLE_LIVE_APIS=1 to skip them entirely. Worth doing when demonstrating
# on a network that blocks outbound requests: searches become instant and
# completely deterministic. Say so if asked - the live literature panel is a
# real feature, it is simply switched off.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# DISABLE_LIVE_APIS=1

# Wall-clock cap per lookup, in seconds.
# LIVE_API_BUDGET=5
# LIVE_API_VALIDATION_BUDGET=2.5

# How long a successful lookup is reused before being fetched again.
# LIVE_API_CACHE_TTL=900

# Set to DEBUG for far more detail when something is not behaving.
# LOG_LEVEL=INFO

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# RESEARCH ASSISTANT
#
# The chat panel answers in one of two ways. With a key set it uses Gemini,
# grounded in the search currently on screen: open conversation, follow-up
# questions, plain-English explanations. Without one it answers from the result
# data by rule - narrower, but truthful and instant, and the panel says which
# answered so a rule-based reply is never presented as a model's.
#
# The key is free and needs no payment card: create one at
# https://aistudio.google.com/apikey. In deployment set it in Render's
# environment settings, never in a committed file. The free tier is
# rate-limited; when the quota is spent the panel falls back rather than
# failing, which is why the fallback is worth having.
GEMINI_API_KEY=

# Model names are retired and added faster than this project will be
# maintained. If the default stops working, the backend log names the HTTP
# error, and the current list is at https://ai.google.dev/gemini-api/docs/models
# GEMINI_MODEL=gemini-2.0-flash
